### [ ] Decide on `sources/.gitkeep`

Currently staged as deleted. It was there to keep an empty directory in git; the
directory has 80 files now, so the deletion is correct — this item exists only so the
call is recorded rather than looking like an accident later.

### [ ] Decide how binary assets live in git

If the repo goes private and `sources/` stays tracked, 288 MB of PNG/JPG enters history
permanently — git does not delta-compress them, and every clone pays for every revision
of every map. Worth considering Git LFS before the first big commit rather than after.
No single file is over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit today, so this is about repo weight,
not a blocker.

